// Functions
// -----------------------------------------------------------------
// 	Simplified definition
Name        :: (parameterName : ParameterType, parameterName : ParameterType) -> (returnName : ReturnType, returnName : ReturnType) {
	// ...
}
// This form is the most simplified form for most day to day use. it will work fine with software and hardware used for defining any procedure, function, operation, block, etc...
// parameters, qualifiers, and return types are optional.

// return types can be named in the functional block declaration.

// if during functional block declaration the a named type is defined using the simplified syntax. then this named type will available to all the callees as if it was independently declared.
//should this even be a thing?
functionalBlockName :: () -> returnName : {
	// ...
}

// this is the same as:
StructName  :: {
	// ...
}

functionalBlockName :: () -> returnName : StructName {
	// ...
}

// This should be the go to syntax for everyone.
// The rest is the for R&D.
// Decisions on what is the implications of each of the specified functional block down blew imply in regard to software/hardware development will be further thought of.







